WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:10.380
Joe Biden had a rough summer in 2021, and
his September and October poll numbers haven’t

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.940
shown much improvement.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.630
Gallup reported recently that Biden’s support
has fallen 14 points since June.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:20.190
He has lost significant ground among politically
consequential independents.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:24.490
Biden’s third quarter polling average is
higher than Donald Trump’s but lower than

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.890
all other presidents Gallup tracks.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:31.039
The president’s ratings have deteriorated
on handling the economy, foreign policy, and

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:32.039
COVID.

00:00:32.039 --> 00:00:35.750
But he has also lost ground on a range of
personal qualities.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.100
In the mid-October Economist/YouGov poll,
38 percent said they liked him.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.470
That was 43 percent in their late January-early
February poll.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:49.460
53 percent in Pew’s September poll said
he cares about the needs of ordinary people.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.380
62 percent gave that response in March.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:57.110
44 percent believe he is mentally sharp, down
from 54 percent.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:00.530
High personal ratings can cushion the impact
of negative performance.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:06.439
It’s early, and President Biden can recover,
but it is harder to pull numbers up than watch

00:01:06.439 --> 00:01:07.692
them go down.

00:01:08.086 --> 00:01:10.275
How well do you think Joe Biden's doing?

00:01:10.275 --> 00:01:16.032
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds.

00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:20.805
And be sure to like and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

